course: dictionary
lesson: 10986
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word warp can mean to bend out of shape, to twist someone's ideas in a bad way, the long threads on a loom, or faster-than-light travel in stories. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «Stare at your own face in dim light for a minute and it can seem to warp and change.» The clues are seem and change, so warp means that something looks bent or twisted out of its normal shape. Scientists have studied this effect, and it happens in your brain.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Put "bend out of shape" in place of warp: "it can seem to bend out of shape and change". It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Warp can be a verb (to warp) or a noun (the warp).
fact: «Warp» means to bend or twist out of shape, often because of heat or water.
fact: In weaving, the warp is the long threads that run lengthwise on a loom; the weft goes across them.
fact: In science fiction, «warp speed» means faster-than-light travel.
fact: Phrases to know: «warp and weft», «time warp», «a warped sense of humour».
exercise: «The wooden shelf began to warp after it got wet.» What does warp mean here? | *To bend or twist out of shape | To count carefully | To stop and rest | To shine brightly
exercise: In weaving, what is the warp? | The threads that go across the loom | *The long threads that run lengthwise on a loom | A wooden frame that holds the loom | A pattern of coloured dots
exercise: «Her warped sense of humour made the others uneasy.» What does warped suggest here? | Very funny and bright | Quick and fast | *Odd, bent away from what is normal | Dry and damp from rain
test: In a science fiction story, what is warp speed? | *Faster-than-light travel | The speed of a bicycle | Walking very slowly | A type of bread
test: Which sentence uses warp to mean bend out of shape? | The spaceship reached warp speed. | She had a warped sense of humour. | *The heat made the plastic lid warp. | The loom has ten warp threads and ten weft threads.
exam: Which is the best way to check your meaning for warp in a sentence? | Look only at the first letter of the word | Ask someone to guess without reading the sentence | Skip the sentence and never come back to it | *Put your meaning in place of warp and see if the sentence still makes sense
